reviewed. In 587 cases the extracted centerline was accepted as it was. In the other 413 the reviewer moved, added or removed endpoints (in 408 cases), edited the mask (in 114) or included a small detached part of the mask (in 3); against a fresh automatic extraction of the same masks, 443 endpoints were added, 221 removed and 380 moved by 2 to \SI{5}{\milli\metre}, and 14 vessel pieces were added. The resulting references contain no loop, 17 detached pieces in 16 cases (median \SI{44}{\milli\metre}, mostly vessels separated in the mask) and 505 terminal branches shorter than \SI{5}{\milli\metre}. Their total length is almost that of the distributed graphs (\SI{630}{} against \SI{638}{\metre} over all cases), with 11{,}582 endpoints against 16{,}866 and 7{,}572 bifurcations against 13{,}572.} The graphs were held fixed throughout, so the perturbation and the metric operated on the same reference graph. This removes extraction quality as a variable and makes each case its own control, so variation between patients does not enter the sample size. Every case distributed with each dataset was used.
