+
+Scores below are the sensitivity $S$ of Equation~\ref{eq:score}: the Spearman correlation between a metric's response and the realised error size, weighted by the median effect size between adjacent severities\rev{, capped at 4; how each result changes at caps of 2 and 1 is given at the end of this section}. Table~\ref{tab:rho-top3} gives, for each error, the three \rev{non-circular} metrics with the highest mean sensitivity across the five datasets, against each dataset in turn; the mean was taken over the datasets that report a score. Cycle disconnection was evaluated on the synthetic dataset alone: TopCoW carries at most two cycles, so severing them gives only one error size, and the aortic and coronary trees have none. The full matrix of every metric against every error, including the node-based metrics below a separating line, is given in Tables~\ref{tab:rho-main} and~\ref{tab:rho-appendix}.
