+| Greedy set cover selects the set (l. 276, 331) | Greedy is perfectly *stable* (1000/1000 paired replicates at cap 4, CV) but not *optimal*: exhaustive search over the 969 triplets prefers the ASCD variant in 1000/1000, even under the manuscript's settings. Under the analytical exclusion at cap 4, greedy never finds the optimum. | Select by exhaustive search (it is cheap); report greedy as the original heuristic. |
+| "A displaced bifurcation was tracked reliably by no metric" (abstract, l. 298, 337, 380, 384) | **Too strong, and partly an artefact.** About 60% of the old total-length response came from the folding perturbation. In the controlled sweep, ASCD and NetMets geom. F1 grade junction displacement monotonically in 100% of cases, even below τ. | Bifurcation shift is graded within a case, but separates poorly across cases. It is the weakest error at caps 4 and 1 (mean best S 0.620 and 0.958) and second-weakest at cap 2 (0.908; missing branch 0.897), so its score level depends on the cap. Endpoint F1 does not see it, and junction F1 is a step detector at about τ. |
+| Circular pairs excluded by zero within-step variance (l. 270) | **Under-excludes.** On the regenerated data it misses total length × disconnection, false loop and missing branch (all five datasets), and × false component and cycle disconnection (synthetic); β0 error × disconnection (all five); and β1 error × false loop (ImageCAS). It flags nothing that the analytical list does not. | The analytical list (Methods), with the reason the CV test fails. |
