+% Hand-written (not generated by make_tables.py). Reconstructed on 2026-10-15
+% from Table A.6 of main_v4.pdf (p. 16), whose source was missing from the
+% repository; wording as printed, citations mapped back to refs.bib keys.
+% One change: the OPT-P row printed "responded like branch coverage F1
+% (correlation 0.80)". No script in the repository computes OPT-P or that
+% correlation, and no source for it was found, so the clause is removed until
+% a source is supplied.
+\begin{table*}[t]
+\centering
+\caption{Metrics from the reviewed literature that were not computed, and the reason.}
+\label{tab:not-computed}
+\footnotesize
+\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{@{}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.27\textwidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.24\textwidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}X@{}}
+\toprule
+Metric & Source & Reason not computed \\
+\midrule
+OF (overlap until first error) & \citet{schaap2009cat08} & Needs single ordered vessels walked from a designated root; a graph has none, so the starting end of each branch would be arbitrary. \\
+OT (overlap, clinically relevant part) & \citet{schaap2009cat08} & Needs the vessel radius at every point; the reference graphs carry no radius. \\
+AI (average inside) & \citet{schaap2009cat08} & Uses the local vessel radius as its cut-off. \\
+CAT08 point correspondence, observer scores and ranking & \citet{schaap2009cat08} & Need single ordered vessels from a root, and several independent annotations of each case. \\
+OPT-J & \citet{citraro2020reliable} & Pools the bifurcation and endpoint matching that Junction F1 and Endpoint F1 report separately. \\
+OPT-P & \citet{citraro2020reliable} & Aligns paths between graphs and measures path continuity, which APLS also covers. \\
+OPT-G, TOPO & \citet{citraro2020reliable}, \citet{biagioni2012topo}, \citet{he2020sat2graph} & Estimated at about 21{,}000 CPU hours for the full sweep (about 27 days on 32 cores). \\
+StreetMover distance (SMD) & \citet{belli2019smd} & One-to-one optimal transport between equal numbers of points; penalises any difference in traced length however closely the curves agree (Table~\ref{tab:similar}). \\
+DIADEM & \citet{gillette2011diadem} & Needs a rooted, directed tree; six thresholds with no published defaults. \\
+Tree and graph edit distance & --- & Use no geometry; intractable on trees with more than about thirty branches. \\
+Dice, clDice, cbDice, ccDice, NSD, surface HD95, Betti matching & \citet{shit2021cldice}, \citet{shi2024cbdice}, \citet{rouge2024ccdice}, \citet{stucki2023topologically} & Defined on masks or surfaces, not on graphs. \\
+NRI & --- & Needs synapse annotations. \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabularx}
+\end{table*}
