+% Hand-written (not generated by make_tables.py). Reconstructed on 2026-10-15
+% from Table A.5 of main_v4.pdf (p. 16), whose source was missing from the
+% repository; wording as printed, citations mapped back to refs.bib keys.
+% The two correlations quoted below were re-checked on the regenerated sweeps
+% (2026-10-15): overlap vs Edge F1 0.956-0.984, number of bifurcations vs
+% branch count ratio 0.933-0.949 (trend-removed profiles, every dataset).
+% SSD row and tree-length-detected row corrected after review (2026-10-15).
+\begin{table*}[t]
+\centering
+\caption{Metrics in the literature that measure the same, or nearly the same, quantity as a metric reported here.}
+\label{tab:similar}
+\footnotesize
+\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{@{}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.27\textwidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}p{0.2\textwidth}>{\raggedright\arraybackslash}X@{}}
+\toprule
+Metric in the literature & Reported here as & Relation \\
+\midrule
+Completeness \citep{wiedemann1998empirical}; length coverage & Edge R & The same quantity: reference length within the tolerance of the prediction, over reference length. \\
+\rev{Tree length detected \citep{lo2012exact,zhang2023atm22}} & \rev{Edge R} & \rev{Close to it, not the same: ATM'22 counts the length of a reference branch only if the branch is detected by the 80\% rule, and computes it on the largest connected component of the prediction.} \\
+Correctness \citep{wiedemann1998empirical} & Edge F1 (precision) & The same quantity: predicted length within the tolerance of the reference, over predicted length. \\
+Quality \citep{wiedemann1998empirical} & Edge F1 & A monotonic function of it when the covered lengths of the two graphs are equal: $Q = \mathrm{F1}/(2 - \mathrm{F1})$. \\
+CL coverage, the graph form of clDice \citep{shit2021cldice} & Edge F1 & The same quantity estimated from points sampled along the curves. \\
+\rev{Spatial distance (SD) and substantial spatial distance (SSD) \citep{peng2010v3d}, as computed in PyNeval \citep{zhang2021pyneval}} & \rev{ASCD} & \rev{SD is a mean distance between the two reconstructions, as ASCD is; SSD averages only the distances above a threshold of two voxels, so it reports how far apart the parts that differ are.} \\
+Overlap OV \citep{schaap2009cat08} & Overlap (OV), Edge F1 & Reported here without CAT08's ordered correspondence and with $\tau$ for the radius; equal to Edge F1 whenever the covered lengths are equal, and correlated above 0.9 with it on all datasets. \\
+Number of components & $\beta_0$ error & Identical on a graph. \\
+Number of bifurcations & Branch count ratio & Responds to the same errors; \rev{trend-removed response profiles correlated at 0.93 to 0.95 on every dataset.} \\
+Critical-node matching \citep{zhang2021pyneval}; node classes of DIADEM and NetMets \citep{gillette2011diadem,mayerich2012netmets} & Junction F1, Endpoint F1 & The same rule: bifurcations and endpoints matched within the tolerance. \\
+Chamfer distance on nodes & ASCD & Its value at the nodes; equal to ASCD as the node spacing goes to zero, and differing from it by the node placement otherwise (Figure~\ref{fig:spacing}). \\
+HD95 on nodes & HD95 & Likewise, at the nodes. \\
+StreetMover distance \citep{belli2019smd} & --- & A different quantity: an optimal-transport distance between equal numbers of points sampled on each graph. It pairs every point with exactly one other, so a prediction longer or shorter than the reference is penalised for the difference in length however closely the curves agree. \\
+\bottomrule
+\end{tabularx}
+\end{table*}
